    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nDetails:\r\n- See PR [42321](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42321) in neovim/neovim\r\n\r\nThat PR also breaks a test in mini.align: \"Align with preview | works | test + args { \"Normal-block\" }\"\r\n\r\nI don't know if the fix needs to be in align, or in test_align. New output:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\n  --|---------|---------|---------|\r\n  01|  a-_-b-_-c                   \r\n  02|aaa-_-bbb_ccc                 \r\n```\r\n\r\nThe old output also aligns on the underscore before the c character:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\n  --|---------|---------|---------|\r\n  01|  a-_-b-_c                    \r\n  02|aaa-_bbb_ccc                  \r\n```\r\n\r\n~~I manually replayed that test with version 0.12.6, and was surprised to see that I could not reproduce the old alignment from the screenshot. The result is always according to the new output...~~\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-15T11:23:36Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am not quite sure, but it *feels* like something got subtly broken in after that PR. In a sense that the new behavior is not something that matches the documentation.\r\n\r\nAs per the test adjustment, I'd rather adjust the position of the target mark instead of the resulting lines. With short comment about why it has to be different on Neovim<0.13 and Neovim>=0.13.\r\n\r\nIn `test_surround.lua` it is for where `a` mark is done: `set_cursor(2, child.fn.has('nvim-0.13') == 1 and 2 or 3)`.\r\n\r\nIn `test_align.lua` (which seems to have the same cause of not the expected) it is through different mark, as mark `a` is\r\nused for other parameters: `child.fn.setpos(\"'b\", { 0, 2, 4, 0 })`.\r\n\r\n> I manually replayed that test with version 0.12.6, and was surprised to see that I could not reproduce the old alignment from the screenshot. The result is always according to the new output...\r\n\r\nI can reproduce it in 0.12.6 as described in the test, so there is okay.",
